 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? I'd mix active learning with passive. Active learning is where you actively use the words, like a quiz, while passive is just reading or listening. Both, actually. A list can be quick to cover lots of words, but random words help you actually remember them. It does, but not as much as you'd think. Pick something fun, like a short story, and read a little every day. A few minutes every day is better than trying to cram whole book in one sitting. Lots of apps have little quiz after each page, so you' actively learning as you go.",
